 up a friendship with a  stripper named jessica over their shared  love of pole dancing  and ends up running to florida for a  two-day bender of drugs prostitution  and murder you know florida stuff  bravo's unique directorial resume  includes lemons with  ex-husband brett gilman as well as the  juneteenth episode of atlanta  she's mainly known for her experimental  festival shorts one of which was a  live-action  virtual reality experience filmed all on  a gopro  so appropriately zola is 82 minutes long  the hollywood reporter  says it makes hustlers look like a  disney movie veering adroitly between  sparkly humor and lynchy and weirdness  and honestly you can't ask for a better  recommendation than that  so mark your calendars because zola  debuts on june 30th  you want to hear a story about how me  and this [ __ ] here fell out  alright friends well that about wraps it  up but be sure to head on over to  rottentomatoes.com to check out our full  list of 15  up-and-coming black directors to look  out for in 2021 and if you have a  suggestion for us  and everyone watching right now please  leave it in the comment section also  don't forget to check out our podcast  rotten tomatoes is wrong  new episodes drop every thursday and we  know you just can't get enough of us  and if you don't want to miss out on any  future episodes of this show be sure to  hit that subscribe button and  notification bell and as always can't  thank you enough for watching the  ketchup  mi nombre is naz perez and we'll see you  guys next time  [Music]  bye  you

